  "details": "As simple as title says. It doesn't show the physbones on the Camera UI preview when you're taking the pictures, but when going through photos in my folder, I found out that all pictures from a session had physbones shown from the moment I enabled the avatar overlay to properly position tail/etc...\n\nSteps to exactly reproduce:\n\nEnable \"Avatar debug overlay\" to \"Proximity physbones\"\n\nOpen camera in stream mode with Spout enabled\n\nApproach physbones with hand\n\nResults into:\n\nOn camera it doesn't show up, but when you take a picture, the file shows the physbones.\n\nTo clarify, in Masking, the UI layer was off (you can see in attached picture that the camera UI, which was directly in front of me, isn't visible)",
